# Every Dockerfile here uses `context: .` (repo root) — without this file, `docker build` sends
# the ENTIRE repo as build context on every build, including every workspace's node_modules, .git
# history, and dist output. Confirmed by hand: a `kuma-provision` build (packages/ops-scripts, a
# few KB of source) took 2.5+ minutes just transferring context before this file existed. None of
# these directories are ever needed inside a Dockerfile — every image does its own `npm install`
# and `npm run db:generate`/build from source.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
